  message: "Merged in PR #2223 (dev 31be103a6; commit 'refactor(core): the identity scheme constants move to a leaf module'). CLOSE CONDITION, re-run on dev 31be103a6: (1) hub_path.py: closure of schema.py = 326 of 1,478 test files (1,477 of 1,477 before; cli.py 314, unchanged); conftest.py -> schema.py: no path. Output: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/hub_dev_31be103a6.txt. (2) Values unchanged: old core against new core on packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src, 1,894 nodes, 0 with a different stable_id / shape_id / fingerprint, same repo_fingerprint (leaf/ids_before_after.txt); the whole suite, id-pin tests included, passed locally under the CI stubs and in PR CI. (3) ADR-0035 and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md name identity_schemes.py. WHAT WAS BUILT IS WIDER THAN THE TITLE: the five scheme constants, value_label, the four labels and identity_digest moved, because analyze/base.py imported them too. Tests: packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_identity_schemes.py; 5 mutations, each one failed test (leaf/mutations.tsv). NOT MEASURED: how often schema.py's import-time code changes. A change to identity_schemes.py's own import-time code still selects the whole suite, by design."  # 2a29
